result:
Confirmed: `createReadRuleSuggestion` returns `PermissionUpdate | undefined` where `PermissionUpdate` is a 6-member discriminated union, but only 3 members (`addRules`/`replaceRules`/`removeRules`) carry `rules`/`behavior`. Accessing those via `?.` without narrowing on `type` fails. Fix is a `type === 'addRules'` guard the flow already guarantees for these inputs.

```json
{"file": "src/packages/permission/src/__tests__/permissionUpdatePure.test.ts",
 "edits": [
   {"old": "    const result = createReadRuleSuggestion('C:\\Users\\me')
    // posix.isAbsolute('C:\\Users\\me') is false → no leading slash added.
    expect(result?.rules[0]?.ruleContent).toBe('C:\\Users\\me/**')",
    "new": "    const result = createReadRuleSuggestion('C:\\Users\\me')
    if (result?.type !== 'addRules') {
      throw new Error('expected addRules')
    }
    // posix.isAbsolute('C:\\Users\\me') is false → no leading slash added.
    expect(result.rules[0]?.ruleContent).toBe('C:\\Users\\me/**')"},
